// The enemy AI's numbers (ticket 0501). Loaded by trpg_content::ai; the rules
// that use them are in trpg_core::ai. Every number is *tunable*: difficulty
// feel is judged in playtest (0804).
//
// An attack's score (the AI makes the highest-scoring attack it can):
//   damage  × expected HP dealt
// + kill    × chance the target falls (0 to 1)
// + lord    if the target is a lord
// − risk    × expected HP taken from the counter
// + terrain × (Def + Avoid / 10) of the tile it attacks from
// Expected values use the forecast's displayed hit chances, follow-ups
// included, crits ignored.
//
// Bosses and combat green units also weigh each attack with every Combat Art
// and combat active they can use (ticket 0503). Using one costs:
// − durability × the durability it costs
// − spell_use  for a spell active (it costs 1 extra spell use)
// so they keep them for attacks they really improve.
//
// What an art or active does beyond the forecast's numbers adds (ticket 0511):
// + debuff    × the points an art's first hit lowers (avoid / 10) × the
//               chance it hits at least once and the target stands
// + stance    × (Def + Res + Avoid / 10) of a stance it doesn't have yet,
//               if a hostile unit could attack its tile this turn
// + post_move   for a move after the attack, from such a tile
// + drain     × min(expected HP dealt / 2, HP it is missing)
//
// Enemies carry no consumables and never drink potions (Nick,
// docs/design/weapons-and-items.md); only healer units heal.
(
    damage: 10,
    kill: 300,
    lord: 50,
    risk: 5,
    terrain: 5,
    durability: 5,
    spell_use: 15,
    debuff: 8,
    stance: 10,
    post_move: 10,
    drain: 5,
)
